=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket is a false premise. A thorough end-to-end investigation of
it_lab3 and every component in its forwarding path found no fault whatsoever.

it_lab3 has the correct IP address (192.168.1.5/24) and default gateway
(192.168.1.1, router0) consistent with all other IT-LAN hosts
(it_hod=.2, it_lab1=.3, it_lab2=.4, it_lab4=.6). Its eth0 interface is
UP/LOWER_UP with no iptables rules in place. ARP resolves the gateway MAC
correctly. The switch serving the IT LAN (switch0) has both bridge ports in
the forwarding state. Ping tests from it_lab3 succeed to: its gateway (0%
loss), a same-LAN peer it_lab1, the servers LAN (pc1, TTL=61 crossing two
router hops), the internet LAN (pc2, TTL=61), and the office LAN (office_pc,
TTL=62). Router0's RIP daemon (ripd) is running under watchfrr supervision, and
its FIB contains all eight expected prefixes fully converged, including the
1.0.0.0/8 (servers), 128.168.0.0/16 (internet), 192.168.3–4.0/24 (office and
principle) subnets learned from downstream routers.

There is no network anomaly. it_lab3 is not isolated; it has full bidirectional
connectivity to every segment in the topology. The user's complaint does not
correspond to any measurable fault in the lab at the time of investigation.

Root cause: The premise of the ticket is incorrect — no configuration or
operational fault exists on it_lab3, its switch port, or the routing
infrastructure.

Corrective action: None required on the network side. The helpdesk ticket
should be closed as "no fault found / false alarm."
=== END ===
